---
tracker:
  kind: linear
  api_key: $LINEAR_API_KEY
  project_slug: my-project-slug-here
  active_states:
    - Todo
    - In Progress
  terminal_states:
    - Done
    - Cancelled
    - Closed
    - Duplicate
polling:
  interval_ms: 30000
workspace:
  root: ~/river-gang-workspaces
  # Optional: clone this repository into each issue workspace. Keep this
  # value in your local WORKFLOW.md; WORKFLOW.md itself is git-ignored.
  repository: https://github.com/your-org/your-repo.git
agent:
  max_concurrent_agents: 2
  max_turns: 20
  max_retry_backoff_ms: 300000
codex:
  command: codex app-server
  approval_policy: never
  turn_sandbox_policy: workspace-write
  turn_timeout_ms: 3600000
  read_timeout_ms: 5000
  stall_timeout_ms: 300000
hooks:
  after_create: ""
  before_run: ""
  after_run: ""
  before_remove: ""
  timeout_ms: 60000
---
You are working on a Linear issue.

Issue: {{ issue.identifier }} — {{ issue.title }}
Current state: {{ issue.state }}

Description:
{{ issue.description }}

Labels: {% for label in issue.labels %}{{ label }} {% endfor %}

{% if attempt > 1 %}
This is attempt {{ attempt }}. Review prior progress in the workspace and continue.
{% endif %}

Use the repository already checked out in this workspace. Create a branch for the Linear issue, commit your changes there, and open a pull request against the same repository. Do not push directly to the default branch.

Use the linear_graphql tool to update the issue when work completes.
